# Links: Always Exact URLs

**Canonical source:** See **docs/COMPREHENSIVE_KNOWLEDGE_DOCUMENT.md** section 5 (URLs and Links). Summary:

**Never give a link without the actual address.**

- **Do not** say "your staging environment", "your host", or "once you deploy" without providing the **exact full URL** the user can open or copy.
- **Do** use the real base URL for this project: **https://www.top10lists.us**
- **Do** give every link as a complete, copy-paste-ready URL (e.g. `https://www.top10lists.us/ai-feed/artifact-payloads-proposed.md`), not a path or a template the user must fill in.
- **Minimize Robert's time testing:** when sharing a link to something that was added or changed, always include the full URL so he can click or paste immediately—no guessing, no inserting.
- **Always make URLs links:** In chat and docs, format every URL as a markdown link `[descriptive text](https://full-url)` so Robert can click them directly. Do not give plain bare URLs when sharing a link—use `[Phoenix city page](https://www.top10lists.us/arizona/phoenix/top10realestateagents)` not just the URL by itself.

**Examples:**
- ✅ [artifact proposal](https://www.top10lists.us/ai-feed/artifact-payloads-proposed.md)
- ✅ [methodology](https://www.top10lists.us/methodology)
- ✅ [Phoenix city page](https://www.top10lists.us/arizona/phoenix/top10realestateagents)
- ✅ Plain URL in code blocks or terminal commands is fine.
- ❌ `https://<your-staging-host>/ai-feed/...`
- ❌ `.../artifact-payloads-proposed.md` (without the full URL when sharing with Robert)
